# AMD64 thunk export spec -- msvcp140.dll.
#
# Added from the 2026-08-15 first-real-game triage: with the application's own
# shipped DLLs now loadable (find_dll_file() searches the load path for the
# guest's machine instead of refusing it outright), what stopped
# quake2ex_steam.exe was Wine builtins with no guest thunk -- each reported as
# c000007b, the loader correctly refusing to splice a native ppc64 module into
# a guest call.  Nothing here is hand-written: the export list comes from this
# module's own .spec.
DLL msvcp140.dll
FROM-SPEC auto

# The 2026-08-17 DOOM triage.  Razer's CChromaEditorLibrary.dll -- the plugin
# DOOM (2016) loads, and the reason mfc140u.dll is in the picture at all --
# imports MSVCP140._Mtx_init_in_situ and called it at PROCESS_ATTACH, straight
# into the sentinel (0xDEAD0004 from CChromaEditorLibrary.dll+0x109b).
#
# Wine implements it (dlls/msvcp90/misc.c:737, void __cdecl (_Mtx_t, int)) but
# declares it in no header, so it takes the .spec location column -- the
# documented downgrade, where the <int|void> column is an unchecked human
# assertion.  "void" is that implementation's own return type.
_Mtx_init_in_situ             0x00000E01  2  void  msvcp140.spec:3682

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The 2026-08-30 Civilization VI triage: THIS FILE IS NOT THE ANSWER FOR CIV VI
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Recorded here because this is where the next reader will look.
#
# Civ VI's run binds 258 per-symbol sentinels across 144 distinct names, and
# 132 of those 144 are MSVCP140 or VCRUNTIME140.  The MSVCP140 half is not
# fixable here and no row should be added for it: the names are MSVC-mangled
# member functions (??6?$basic_ostream@DU?$char_traits@D@std@@@std@@QEAAAEAV01@H@Z
# and ~110 more), plus VTABLE DATA (??_7ios_base@std@@6B@,
# ??_7?$basic_ios@DU?$char_traits@D@std@@@std@@6B@) and a DATA CONSTANT
# (?_BADOFF@std@@3_JB).  A trap stub is a function; there is no arity or return
# type to assert for a vtable, and no amount of .spec-location downgrade makes
# one, so even a perfect oracle would refuse them.
#
# The answer is the one msvcp100 and msvcp120 already take: stage a REAL
# x86-64 build of the module into the prefix's C:\windows\sysx8664 and let it
# run as a guest module under the emulator.  ppc64le/steamtool/stage-guest-runtime
# does that now for every launch, sourcing the file from any Proton
# installation's own dist tree rather than from an app prefix the title may not
# have.  Verified before shipping it: all 97 kernel32, 1 ntdll, 82 ucrtbase and
# 12 vcruntime140 imports of that module are served by this tree's guest
# thunks, so unlike the msvcr100 attempt it does not die in its own
# PROCESS_ATTACH.  (One of the twelve, __uncaught_exception, was a hole until
# that same pass -- see dlls/vcruntime140/vcruntime140.thunks.)
#
# The VCRUNTIME140 half IS fixable here-adjacent and was fixed properly rather
# than staged over; see that file's 2026-08-30 banner for why replacing the
# module wholesale would have cost the guest C++ exception personality.
#
# TWO THINGS THE STAGED MODULE STILL ASKS FOR AND DOES NOT GET, both measured
# on 2026-08-30 and both non-fatal at load (EOSSDK, DatabaseDLL_FinalRelease
# and Localization_FinalRelease all loaded clean with both missing):
#
#   concrt140.dll -- msvcp140's DllMain LoadLibraryA's it (dlls/msvcp90/
#       msvcp_main.c, init_cxx_funcs at :267) and pulls
#       Context::IsCurrentTaskCollectionCanceling out of it.  It logged
#       `load_dll Failed to load module L"concrt140.dll"; status=c000007b`
#       -- the loader refusing this tree's native ppc64 builtin for a guest
#       call, since Concurrency:: is another mangled C++ ABI with no useful
#       thunk.  CLOSED: stage-guest-runtime stages it too, and its 36
#       kernel32 / 3 ntdll / 19 ucrtbase imports are all served.
#
#   ucrtbase._set_new_handler -- GetProcAddress'd by the same function, and
#       STILL ABSENT ON PURPOSE.  spec2thunk refuses it because its return is
#       a function pointer, not because of the argument; the .spec-location
#       downgrade would get past that.  What must not be got past is the
#       ARGUMENT: it is a guest `int (__cdecl *)(size_t)` handed to native
#       code that will later call it, so an ordinary row would leave native
#       ppc64 doing `bctrl` on a guest address.  That is what the callback
#       rows in dlls/msvcr100/msvcr100.thunks and the registration-
#       interception table in dlls/ntdll/signal_ppc64.c exist to prevent, and
#       closing this means a row in BOTH plus a line in
#       ppc64le/seh/check-crt-callbacks.sh.  Until then, absent is the safe
#       state: msvcp140 stores NULL and only a game that actually calls
#       std::set_new_handler is affected, whereas a naive row would corrupt
#       any game that does.
